You're in great shape, you really don't need to worry. Here are the
important things you need to do:

1) Make sure the important stuff that needs to be blessed, is blessed.
Here's what you want to have blessed:
1a) bag of holding
1b) whatever remove curse scrolls you have
1c) unicorn horn

Make sure you realize that a lot of things that are useful become
significantly more useful when blessed. Remove curse, when uncursed,
uncurses whatever you're wielding, cursed armor, rings, and amulets
(and maybe a lodestone if you have it I don't recall). When blessed,
however, it gets every single cursed item in you inventory...
obviously much more useful. The same goes for genocide. Uncursed
genocide gets one named monster (i.e. Lich), but with blessed, you can
just type L and it gets rid of all 4 types of L.

Here's the order in which I recommend to genocide monsters:

L - curses your stuff, purple L teleport to and from the upstairs to
heal which is annoying. They have other spells too, but at your power
level summon nasties isn't too dangerous and you have MR so destroy
armor won't work. But short on holy water, get rid of those L!
h - makes you unid stuff, forget levels, int drain, gets many attacks.
Not THAT nasty if you can grease your helmet and are careful about
writing Elbereth, but still a big pain, especially on water levels
where you can't write E.
; - instakill attack. Again not that nasty if you can grease your
cloak but still annoying, especially on the plane of water.
R - disenchanters remove enchantment from weapons and armor

That's about it for the really nasty stuff. I also if not doing
genoless like to genocide m before Orcus-town to generate more loot.
But that's usually not that necessary.

2) if you don't have any remove curse scrolls, and you don't have a
wand of polymorph, wish for it and polypile your scrolls. It sounds
like you have been using holy water to uncurse stuff, that's extremely
inefficient when you can do it in bulk with remove curse. Also don't
forget about cancellation, cancellation wands turn any item into the
uncursed +0 form of itself (blanks scrolls, most potions become
water). One game I found cursed -4 gauntlets of power, one zap,
uncursed +0 :)

3) Start collecting every single scroll and potion you find, for the
above polypiling and also for diluting to make more water to water
pray / dip into more holy water.

4) This is minor, but don't carry around 2 BoH. Just increases the
chance you'll screw up and blow them up... and there's no limit to how
much stuff you can put in a BoH, except for the stuff that makes them
explode and the heavy containers (which I guess are too big to fit
through the opening).

5) Mjollnir is fine. There aren't that many shock resistant monsters,
and the ones that are shock resistant aren't usually the nastiest. The
Plane of Air will be a pain but just run around stuff instead of
attacking it there. You should #twoweapon with a long sword in the off
hand until you can find a silver saber. There's usually one in the
castle at your experience level (being wielded by one of the high
level soldiers). If not, polypile weapons when you're polypiling the
useless scrolls.

6) You're going to want to spend almost all of your remaining wishes
on magic markers and wands of polymorph, possibly saving a wish for a
cockatrice corpse on astral.

7) Food. Looks like you are short on food, there's plenty in the
castle. Don't worry about it unless you are about to starve.

8) If you don't have a source of levitation at this point, that's not
a bad thing to use a spare wish on (get the ring not the boots)... but
if you have junk rings you should just polypile them when you're doing
the other polypiling first. Worst case scenario, dig through the floor
in Medusa's level and come back up, shatter Perseus statue, it has a
good chance of having levitation boots.

9) Don't worry about wand collection, ring collection is more
important. Here are the rings you want, IMO, in order of importance:

Most important:
Levitation
Free Action
Conflict
Slow Digestion

Less important:
Increase Damage
Regeration (don't wear this unless you need it! Consumes nutrition
like a ring of hunger)
Teleport Control (if you don't have the intrinsic)

Not important but still useful:
Polymorph / Polymorph control set (not that important but nice to
have)
Gain Constitution (carrying capacity)
Adornment (foocubus dancing)

10) I wouldn't spend too much more effort on enchanting up armor.
Instead I would focus more on getting magic mapping scrolls for
gehennom. They are very cheap and will make your life much easier.

11) This may be a dumb question, but have you been using blessed
charging scrolls on your wands of wishing? I would think you should
have more stuff than you do with 2 /oW. Use blessed, though, because
only blessed guarantees 3 wishes. Uncursed is 1-3. Also, both uncursed
and blessed charging set an empty (0:xx) marker to (1:50).
11a) Also attempting to zap a (1:0) wand of wishing has a 1/121 chance
of getting another wish. So if you zap it and then press Ctrl+A
repeatedly you'll eventually get another wish, (and the wand
disintegrates) don't forget about that.

Good luck!

